## What happened since your first evaluation

Your first evaluation raised nine findings (six P1, three P2). All nine were reconciled
and every one was accepted — none was refuted. What changed, so you can judge the fixes
rather than re-derive the findings:

1. **Ingest trusted caller labels.** Captures now report `observed_connector_types` (from
   the platform's execution-connector rows, sentinels excluded) and `observed_method`
   (from the operation component, because the platform reports one generic action for all
   eight verbs). `ingest()` reconciles the declared family and action against both and
   REFUSES a mismatch. A REST HEAD capture declared as `family="database"` now raises.

2. **Registry affirmed unmapped families.** `retry_safety()` resolves through the
   vocabulary first; a family no live connector maps onto returns `unverified` regardless
   of what an evidence row says. Operation records are now TYPED
   (`OperationContractRecordV1`), so an untyped dict no longer loads.

3. **§5.B's model set was absent.** Now built: `ContractKeySemanticsDefinitionV1`,
   `ComponentProjectionAllowlistV1`, `CaptureReferenceV1`, `LiveComponentIdentityV1`,
   `StaticRouteCoverageV1`, `ServiceWideRouteCoverageV1`, `OperationContractRecordV1`, and
