- Attest every consumed grant for every process root; enforce nested account scope equals the parent attestation scope.

Apply sequencing:

- Perform a global read-only recheck of all evidence-bound operation/connection identities immediately before the first mutation.
- Recheck again after late binding immediately before each evidence-bound submission.
- For structured update, add a pre-submit callback after merge/materialization and before the platform update call.
- Compare ID, explicit version, and config digest independently. A credential-only version advance fails even when the credential-excluding digest is unchanged.
- Pre-submit drift/unavailability refuses that pending submission.
- After a successful or mutation-uncertain submission, read back both operation and connection and compare against the pinned identity:
  - match: normal success;
  - drift: named reconciliation failure;
  - unavailable: named reconciliation failure.
- A post-submit failure retains component ID, platform result, readback/uncertainty state, mutation accounting, and evidence attestation. It never implies rollback.
