## Risks

- The named source golden is actually a target-call golden. Reusing it literally for a source connector would encode a false acceptance criterion; add the independent source-role oracle.
- Source-role dynamic path must use generalized `ConnectorCallNodeV1`. Adding a prefix before legacy `SourceEndpointV1` would widen a settled grammar and conflict with #154/#160.
- Binding-present XML affects `<parameters>`, `<dynamicProperties>`, and potentially graph shape ordinals. Binding-absent bytes must remain exact; the existing renderer should not be edited.
- `source_replay_policy` changes canonical JSON/fingerprints because defaults are serialized, although emitted XML stays unchanged.
- Capability fields, diagnostics, retry policy, discovery output, and schema-template projections are served contracts; update all frozen snapshots/parity tests atomically.
- New capability rows and replay-safety flips change the abstract compiler revision. With the current global revision model this rotates all process fingerprints, not only plans using the changed connector.
- Concrete evidence identities must never enter relocatable fingerprints. Conversely, excluding them from mutation attestations would break auditability.
- The outer workflow hash is account-bound; only the per-process relocatable fingerprint can satisfy the two-account equality test.
- Existing mutation attestations already contain top-level account scope, so two accounts cannot yield attestations differing solely in the new tuple.
- A pre-submit race can occur after earlier plan mutations. Preserve partial mutation accounting and use reconciliation semantics rather than promising transactionality or rollback.
- Live readbacks must be performed once into a trusted snapshot and reused; re-deriving identity from caller config or at independent call sites reopens the GET/POST bypass.
- Connection version remains authoritative even though credential material is excluded from the configuration digest.
- The exact live grammar for Boomi execution/component identifiers is not established in the issue. Do not weaken validators to accept arbitrary strings; pin a versioned closed grammar from the first admissible capture before adding production records.
- Projection allowlists may initially reject legitimate new platform XML. That false-negative is intentional; unknown content must block minting until reviewed and versioned.
- QName-aware canonicalization requires namespace-context-aware parsing. A plain `ElementTree.fromstring` projection will lose binding-only namespace declarations and is not acceptable.
- The repo has no wheel packaging. The deployment-relevant proof is an actual Docker-image package-resource import; adding unrelated wheel infrastructure is not part of #155.
- `verified_action` alone currently authorizes an idempotent-write row. Keeping that behavior would contradict the issue’s per-call sole-authority requirement; require a typed grant for all positive write classes.
- The four actual symbol-table call sites and both reconstruction helpers must migrate together. Missing any one recreates caller-authoritative or grant-dropping behavior.
- `.gitignore` needs both directory and recursive-content negations; otherwise the derived report can remain silently ignored.
- Apply-path changes touch mutation accounting and update preservation. All pre/post failure tests must assert retained IDs, results, readbacks, and attestations—not merely diagnostic codes.

